\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{, denoted by $J_{x,c}^{\text {eff}}$. This quantity can subsequently be used as an input quantity in a macroscopic fracture criterion such as\nobreakspace {}(\ref {eq:fracture_criterion_J}).}}{5}{section*.57}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Such a use is justified only to the extent that the fracture process analyzed by\nobreakspace {}(\ref {eq:fracture_criterion_J}) is representative of the specific material and loading situation considered in the numerical experiment.}}{5}{section*.58}%
