\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{For this fixed wall width, the ordering can be interpreted through the different resistance against crack re-nucleation and the additional energy dissipated during ligament failure; in particular, once the one-dimensional tensile strength is largely eliminated as the dominant difference between models, the enhanced dissipation appears to play an important role. The following parameter study shows that this ordering is representative of the main trend, while the detailed pore interaction length additionally depends on $w_s$.}}{20}{section*.157}%
