\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Nevertheless, Figs.\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:position_3D} and\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:PAPER_VM_Jx_all_3D} still show phases of nearly instantaneous crack advance and elevated values of the J-Integral when the crack front is forced to pass between pores. The comparison in Fig.\nobreakspace {}\ref {fig:PAPER_06b_Jx_vs_wsteg_2D_3D} therefore indicates that this mechanism still produces a toughening effect of comparable magnitude to the two-dimensional case.}}{24}{section*.202}%
